skills.body:
Write one file, deck.html, in the deck's folder. Put the base CSS below and then the chosen theme's CSS (from the themes collection) in a <style>. Each slide is <section class="slide [title|section|quote]">. Use the classes below for layouts: .kicker, h1/h2, ul.points, .cols (and .cols.wide-left), .big, .card, .grid3, figure/figcaption, .footer (slide number and the deck's short name on every slide but the title). No external scripts, fonts or images from the network (the renderer has none): inline SVG for charts and icons, local files for images.

To see it: kit_run kit decks-render, tool slides, args {html: "<folder>/deck.html", out: "<folder>/slides"}, then read each slides/slide-NN.png (tool slide, with n, for one slide). To print it: tool pdf, args {html: "<folder>/deck.html", out: "<folder>/deck.pdf"}; tool pptx makes deck.pptx the same way, when PowerPoint is wanted.

Base CSS:

```css
/* deck base: every slide is a 1280×720 section; the theme sets the variables. */
@page { size: 1280px 720px; margin: 0; }
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
html, body { background: #888; }
body { font-family: var(--font-body); color: var(--fg); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
.slide { width: 1280px; height: 720px; overflow: hidden; position: relative; background: var(--bg); margin: 0 auto 24px;
  padding: 72px 88px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; break-after: page; page-break-after: always; }
@media print { html, body { background: none; } .slide { margin: 0; } }
.kicker { font: 600 18px/1.2 var(--font-body); letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 20px; }
h1 { font: var(--display-weight) 72px/1.05 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.02em; }
h2 { font: var(--display-weight) 44px/1.15 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.01em; margin-bottom: 36px; max-width: 1000px; }
p, li { font-size: 26px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--fg); }
.muted { color: var(--muted); }
ul.points { list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 22px; }
ul.points li { padding-left: 32px; position: relative; }
ul.points li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .6em; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--accent); }
.cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 56px; flex: 1; align-items: start; }
.cols.wide-left { grid-template-columns: 3fr 2fr; }
.big { font: var(--display-weight) 160px/1 var(--font-display); color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: -.03em; }
.footer { position: absolute; left: 88px; right: 88px; bottom: 32px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
.slide.title { justify-content: flex-end; padding-bottom: 110px; }
.slide.title h1 { max-width: 1000px; }
.slide.title .sub { font-size: 30px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 24px; max-width: 900px; }
.slide.section { justify-content: center; background: var(--accent-bg); }
.slide.section h1 { color: var(--accent-fg); }
.slide.quote { justify-content: center; }
.slide.quote blockquote { font: italic 44px/1.3 var(--font-display); max-width: 1000px; }
.slide.quote cite { display: block; margin-top: 28px; font-size: 22px; color: var(--muted); font-style: normal; }
.card { background: var(--surface); border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px 32px; }
.grid3 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 28px; }
figure { flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; }
figure svg { flex: 1; width: 100%; height: auto; }
figcaption { font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 12px; }
```

templates.prompt:
Revise a delivered deck. Its record and the user's notes:

{{input}}

Use the deck skills. Open the deck's folder, change deck.html as the notes ask, review the changed slides (kit_run decks-render, tool slide, then read it; deck-review), print the PDF again (tool pdf), publish both files again (a new version), and update the record.
